{
  "$comment": "ADR-0001 content-transport benchmark \u2014 the preregistered constants (resolution plan \u00a74.3 step 1, \u00a74.4, \u00a74.5, \u00a74.8). Every value is LITERAL by design: the workload is a function of (config, repo, SHA) and all three are pinned. Values marked 'production literal' mirror module-local constants in scripts/*.ts and are cross-checked by benchConfig.test.ts where the production symbol is exported. After \u00a78 ratification this file is FROZEN \u2014 any change invalidates affected timing data and requires a plan amendment plus one adversarial review round.",
  "benchmark": "adr-0001-content-transport",
  "planRef": "docs/plans/adr-0001-disagreements-resolution.md",
  "githubHost": "github.com",
  "reps": 5,
  "drivers": [
    "T0",
    "T1",
    "T2a",
    "T2c"
  ],
  "selection": {
    "$comment": "The production selection function's pinned inputs (\u00a74.3): scanUnit/locateManifests/classifyFile are reused directly, so the classifier terms are the production code itself; these are the config-shaped inputs it takes. trackedPackages was finalised at corpus pinning (pre-freeze, plan \u00a74.2's C2 \u2264~500 preference): react resolves in C1/prometheus's web/ui (a genuine source class); pino is fastify-ecosystem coverage; typescript/eslint/semver were deliberately EXCLUDED \u2014 C2/nest declares them, which made every .ts file source-selected (1,785 reads measured) and would have pushed every C2 API-driver run into multi-window segmentation.",
    "trackedPackages": [
      "react",
      "pino"
    ],
    "excludeDirGlobs": [
      "**/node_modules/**",
      "**/dist/**",
      "**/build/**",
      "**/vendor/**"
    ],
    "maxScanBytes": 2097152
  },
  "rest": {
    "rawAccept": "application/vnd.github.raw+json",
    "attemptCap": 6,
    "secondaryBaseWaitMs": 60000,
    "transientBaseWaitMs": 2000
  },
  "restFallbackBudget": {
    "$comment": "Per-unit REST fallback budget, EVERY driver (\u00a74.4): max(floor, ceil(fractionOfSelected \u00d7 selected)). Exhaustion is a unit failure (G2).",
    "floor": 20,
    "fractionOfSelected": 0.1,
    "rounding": "ceil"
  },
  "t1": {
    "aliasCap": 250,
    "queryDocBytesCap": 49152,
    "batchContentBytesCap": 1572864,
    "argvBytesCap": 131072,
    "aliasSelection": "object(expression: $EXPR) { __typename ... on Blob { oid byteSize isBinary isTruncated text } }",
    "rateLimitRider": "rateLimit { cost remaining resetAt }",
    "splitTriggers": {
      "graphqlErrorType": "TIMEOUT",
      "timeoutMessageRegex": "\\btimed?[ -]?out\\b",
      "timeoutMessageRegexFlags": "i",
      "consecutive5xx": {
        "count": 2,
        "statuses": [
          502,
          503,
          504
        ],
        "bodies": "empty-or-non-json",
        "capUtilisationFloor": 0.8
      }
    },
    "split": {
      "maxDepth": 2,
      "maxDescendantsPerOriginal": 4
    },
    "circuitBreakerConsecutiveFailedDispatches": 3
  },
  "t2a": {
    "$comment": "Size-based api-escape (\u00a74.4): a unit whose PINNED REST repository size (KB, recorded in corpus.json at pinning \u2014 size rides discovery, which the benchmark excludes as identical across drivers) exceeds this threshold routes to per-file REST with T0 semantics \u2014 EXCEPT truncated trees, which must clone anyway (the oversized-and-truncated hole is exhibited, not patched). Derivation: predicted clone+checkout disk \u2248 2 \u00d7 size, so the escape aligns with the 2 GiB G4 gate at size > 1 GiB = 1048576 KB.",
    "apiEscapeRepoSizeKb": 1048576
  },
  "spawn": {
    "$comment": "production literals: SPAWN_TIMEOUT_MS / SPAWN_KILL_GRACE_MS are exported and cross-checked; outputCapBytes mirrors github.ts's module-local MAX_SPAWN_OUTPUT_BYTES (110 MiB).",
    "timeoutMs": 900000,
    "killGraceMs": 2000,
    "outputCapBytes": 115343360
  },
  "frame": {
    "$comment": "Framed seam limits (\u00a73.1/\u00a73.2). frameCeilingBytes = production's spawn-output cap, the absolute per-frame ceiling; the per-frame bound is the ls-tree-declared size exactly. childPoolSize = the subprocess semaphore's production default (\u00a73.1 \u2014 a small fixed pool, never one-per-unit).",
    "maxHeaderBytes": 256,
    "frameCeilingBytes": 115343360,
    "stderrRingBytes": 65536,
    "readDeadlineMs": 60000,
    "disposeDeadlineMs": 10000,
    "childPoolSize": 8
  },
  "lsTree": {
    "maxEntries": 1000000,
    "maxRecordBytes": 65536,
    "maxOutputBytes": 115343360
  },
  "protocol": {
    "$comment": "\u00a74.5. Cold = no api_cache rows, no reused clones, no HTTP cache; DNS/TLS warmth is ambient. Washout = max(floorMs, longest outstanding throttle horizon from the previous run). Temp prefix pa-bench-* \u2014 NOT pkg-audit-*, which production's startup sweep deletes unconditionally (github.ts:2096).",
    "tempPrefix": "pa-bench-",
    "washoutFloorMs": 60000,
    "diskGateBytes": 2147483648,
    "diskSamplerHz": 1,
    "g4AttributableSecondarySignals": {
      "pass": 0,
      "warnAtMost": 1,
      "failAt": 2
    },
    "rerunAllowancePerUnitDriver": 1,
    "fidelityBattery": {
      "when": "after-matrix",
      "repsPerFixtureDriver": 1
    }
  },
  "budget": {
    "$comment": "\u00a74.8 worst-case reservation. P_max is a FROZEN ASSUMPTION: any measured per-request cost above it, or any run overrunning its own WC, halts the matrix (R5 freeze repair). rate_limit reads are excluded (documented as not counting against the REST primary limit). Formulas (evaluated in benchBudget.ts): REST WC_core = (contentRequests + treeRequests + fallbackBudget) \u00d7 attemptCap + attemptCap (the \u00a74.4 SHA-classifier attempt-loop allowance) + fixedPerRunOverheadRequests; GraphQL WC_graphql = plannedBatches \u00d7 (1 + maxDescendantsPerOriginal) \u00d7 attemptCap \u00d7 pMax.",
    "pMaxPointsPerGraphqlAttempt": 10,
    "headroomFactor": 1.1,
    "bucketCapacityPerHour": 5000,
    "fixedPerRunOverheadRequests": 0
  },
  "noiseBand": {
    "$comment": "\u00a74.7: band = max(floor, pilot max/min wall ratio rounded UP to the next roundUpTo).",
    "floor": 1.25,
    "roundUpTo": 0.05
  },
  "pilot": {
    "driver": "T0",
    "slot": "C2",
    "reps": 5
  },
  "williamsRows": [
    [
      "T0",
      "T1",
      "T2c",
      "T2a"
    ],
    [
      "T1",
      "T2a",
      "T0",
      "T2c"
    ],
    [
      "T2a",
      "T2c",
      "T1",
      "T0"
    ],
    [
      "T2c",
      "T0",
      "T2a",
      "T1"
    ],
    [
      "T0",
      "T2a",
      "T1",
      "T2c"
    ]
  ],
  "williamsFifthRowNote": "Rows 1-4 are a digram-balanced 4\u00d74 Williams square (each driver once per position; each ordered predecessor pair exactly once). Row 5 is the declared fifth order: its three digrams (T0\u2192T2a, T2a\u2192T1, T1\u2192T2c) each already occur exactly once in rows 1-4, so no ordered pair reaches three occurrences \u2014 the minimum any fifth row can achieve.",
  "scaffolding": {
    "$comment": "SHA-pinned acquisition scaffolding (\u00a74.4) \u2014 bench scaffolding, NOT proposed production grammar. Slots in {braces} are substituted before the spawn module compares argv verbatim. The gitconfig is the bench's pinned generated config (mirroring production's ensureGitConfig approach: credential helper delegating to gh, https-only protocol) plus the ONE probe-varied knob, core.autocrlf (baseline false; the checkout-config probe rep runs true).",
    "tuples": {
      "init": [
        "init",
        "--template=",
        "--object-format={objectFormat}",
        "{dest}"
      ],
      "remoteAdd": [
        "remote",
        "add",
        "origin",
        "{url}"
      ],
      "fetch": [
        "fetch",
        "--depth",
        "1",
        "--no-tags",
        "--no-recurse-submodules",
        "origin",
        "{sha}"
      ],
      "checkoutDetach": [
        "checkout",
        "--detach",
        "FETCH_HEAD"
      ],
      "lsRemoteProbe": [
        "ls-remote",
        "{url}",
        "refs/heads/{branch}"
      ]
    },
    "gitconfigBaseline": "[credential]\n\thelper = !{ghBin} auth git-credential\n[protocol]\n\tallow = never\n[protocol \"https\"]\n\tallow = always\n[core]\n\tautocrlf = false\n",
    "gitconfigProbeAutocrlfTrue": "[credential]\n\thelper = !{ghBin} auth git-credential\n[protocol]\n\tallow = never\n[protocol \"https\"]\n\tallow = always\n[core]\n\tautocrlf = true\n"
  },
